    {
      "startFrame": 0,
      "endFrame": 30,
      "text": "Did you know"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 30,
      "endFrame": 60,
      "text": "Spain is the country"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 60,
      "endFrame": 96,
      "text": "with the strangest borders?"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 96,
      "endFrame": 135,
      "text": "On the map, it looks like Spain"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 135,
      "endFrame": 180,
      "text": "has only two land neighbors,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 180,
      "endFrame": 216,
      "text": "France and Portugal,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 216,
      "endFrame": 270,
      "text": "but in reality there are many more."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 270,
      "endFrame": 330,
      "text": "Just the border with France"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 330,
      "endFrame": 390,
      "text": "creates a few unusual oddities."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 390,
      "endFrame": 450,
      "text": "For example, the town of Llivia,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 450,
      "endFrame": 510,
      "text": "which lies entirely within French territory,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 510,
      "endFrame": 570,
      "text": "only 2 kilometers from the border,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 570,
      "endFrame": 630,
      "text": "but it is Spanish territory."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 630,
      "endFrame": 690,
      "text": "This phenomenon is called an enclave."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 690,
      "endFrame": 765,
      "text": "Further west, you'll find an even more surprising case:"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 765,
      "endFrame": 825,
      "text": "Pheasant Island."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 825,
      "endFrame": 915,
      "text": "Spain and France couldn't agree on how to divide it"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 915,
      "endFrame": 990,
      "text": "because the border ran right through the middle,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 990,
      "endFrame": 1050,
      "text": "so they decided to take turns owning it."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1050,
      "endFrame": 1140,
      "text": "For the first half of the year it belongs to Spain,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1140,
      "endFrame": 1245,
      "text": "and for the second half, the border shifts to France."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1245,
      "endFrame": 1335,
      "text": "There is also another neighbor hidden between them: Andorra."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1335,
      "endFrame": 1455,
      "text": "One of the smallest countries, with a population of 80,000"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1455,
      "endFrame": 1560,
      "text": "and almost half the size of New York City."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1560,
      "endFrame": 1665,
      "text": "Spain has another hidden neighbor: the United Kingdom."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1665,
      "endFrame": 1815,
      "text": "Britain holds an overseas territory at the tip of Iberia:"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1815,
      "endFrame": 1995,
      "text": "Gibraltar — a centuries-old dispute between Spain and the UK"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1995,
      "endFrame": 2130,
      "text": "controlling access to the Mediterranean via the Strait of Gibraltar."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 2130,
      "endFrame": 2235,
      "text": "The strait divides two continents: Europe and Africa."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 2235,
      "endFrame": 2355,
      "text": "Yet Spain is the only European country with a land border in Africa,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 2355,
      "endFrame": 2475,
      "text": "thanks to three Spanish enclaves bordering Morocco."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 2475,
      "endFrame": 2580,
      "text": "Two are the cities of Ceuta and Melilla,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 2580,
      "endFrame": 2715,
      "text": "and the third is Peñón de Vélez de la Gomera, once an island"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 2715,
      "endFrame": 2820,
      "text": "connected to the mainland by a narrow isthmus,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 2820,
      "endFrame": 2898,
      "text": "creating the shortest land border in the world — just 85 meters long."
    }
  ],
